# Review: PipelinePlugin

The board itself works. The `Pipeline` type (in `@dxos/types`), the article, the composable
`PipelineComponent` with column drag-and-drop, and the `PipelineProperties` column editor (add, rename,
delete, reorder, query) exist and do roughly what the spec says. Almost none of it is tested: the only test,
`plugin.test.ts`, checks that the schema module activates, and the three stories render without play
functions.

Much of the spec is missing or diverged. The plugin contributes no app-graph builder, so there are no
"Invocations" or "Automation" companions (F-1.4, F-6). Items cannot be dragged between columns, and
`Column.order` is never read (F-4.2). Every column is listed newest-first, including space queries
(F-3.3). The research template is not in this plugin: it is a plugin-debug space-generator preset that throws
on a missing mailbox instead of returning null (F-5). Creation is a `CreateObjectEntry`, not an operation,
and does not pass `hidden: true`.

Of 34 items: 0 done, 14 untested, 3 partial, 6 diverged, 11 missing.

